i=A.bh(d7,1,"For the Universal system (Zodiac): Here we consider our Solar System as a whole, nested within its parent system\u2014the Galaxy. At this scale, the maximum significant interaction is of a structural-gravitational nature. It is the constant alignment of our entire system with respect to the Galactic Center (GC). Therefore, the spatial vector pointing to the GC becomes the fundamental anchor for the universal coordinate system of the Zodiac.")
h=A.bh(d7,2,"For the Local system (Houses): Here we consider the subjective experience of a person at a specific point on Earth, nested within the parent system\u2014the Solar System, represented by the Sun. At this scale, the maximum interaction is of an energy-cyclical nature. It manifests not as a static direction, but as the peak event of the daily cycle\u2014the moment when the vector to the Sun crosses the local meridian [MC]. This is the point of receiving maximum energy, light, and heat, which determines the rhythms of survival and activity. Therefore, it is the culmination event of this vector that becomes the anchor for the local coordinate system of the Houses.")
