f8=A.N(h0,'Objective Orb: A Theoretical Construct.\nJustification: At the deepest level, there is an objective, physical "width" of resonance between two cycles within the [Field] itself. It can be calculated from the ratio of their periods and may be fractions of a degree. This is the theoretical, perfectly precise peak of interaction that underlies the phenomenon. It is the "true signal," but for practical analysis, it must be viewed through the prism of human perception of time, which is not instantaneous.\nCalculation: The orb of interaction between two planets (Planet A and Planet B) is directly proportional to the ratio of their orbital periods. The smaller period is divided by the larger one. This gives us a coefficient from 0 to 1, which shows "what fraction of its path the outer planet travels while the inner one completes one revolution."')
