B.aXT=new A.d('After a stimulus has been instinctively "felt" (the Moon) and intellectually "identified" (Mercury), the stage of forming a subjective attitude begins. Venus marks this very process\u2014a secondary, sensory evaluation that answers the question, "Do I like this? Is it beautiful? Is it valuable to me?".\n\nIt translates the primary lunar impulse of "comfort" into a more complex aesthetic feeling, and the Mercurian fact into a personal preference. Its slower cycle (~8 months) ideally corresponds not to an instant reaction, but to the process of forming stable values and attachments\u2014developing relationships, realizing creative projects, accumulating what we consider beautiful and valuable. Venus creates our "value compass," which determines all our subsequent choices.',null,B.b,null,null)
