B.aOU=new A.d('One "recipe"\u2014four completely different "dishes." This leads us to the first question: if the same astrological "cause" produces mutually exclusive effects, can we even call it a cause?\n\nBut the problem is deeper. Let\'s invite two astrologers from the same school. One, based on their experience, will see the potential for a strong family in this placement. The other, recalling a different client, will emphasize the risk of passive aggression. Both pieces of advice may be wise, but they are different. This reveals the second problem: the interpretation of the chart is colored by the personality and experience of the astrologer themselves.\n\nThe result is a double blow to objectivity: the client can express the energy in countless ways, and the astrologer can interpret it through the lens of their own worldview. This proves that the supposed mechanism of "influence," as presented by astropsychology, simply does not exist.',null,B.b,null,null)
