B.aRI=new A.d("Jupiter, as the first and largest of the gas giants, marks a qualitative leap in time scale compared to the personal planets. Its active cycle phase, or Planning Horizon, is about 6 years.\n\nThis six-year period elevates a person to a new level of interaction with the world\u2014the level of social integration, horizon expansion, and the formation of a broader worldview. If Mars's one-year horizon corresponds to tactical actions, Jupiter's six-year horizon allows for the implementation of medium-term social strategies:\n\n\u2022 To obtain higher education and find a first serious job.\n\u2022 To achieve significant career growth within one company or project.\n\u2022 To develop a business from a startup to a stable enterprise.\n\u2022 To fully adapt and establish oneself in a new country or social environment.\n\nThus, Jupiter correlates with the principle of growth, expansion, optimism, and the aspiration to find one's authoritative place in a larger social or ideological system. The full 12-year cycle includes a subsequent phase of integrating this experience and reflecting on the social status achieved.",null,B.b,null,null)
