B.atU=s(["\u043f\u0440\u0432\u043e \u0442\u0440\u043e\u043c\u0435\u0441\u0435\u0447\u0458\u0435","\u0432\u0442\u043e\u0440\u043e \u0442\u0440\u043e\u043c\u0435\u0441\u0435\u0447\u0458\u0435","\u0442\u0440\u0435\u0442\u043e \u0442\u0440\u043e\u043c\u0435\u0441\u0435\u0447\u0458\u0435","\u0447\u0435\u0442\u0432\u0440\u0442\u043e \u0442\u0440\u043e\u043c\u0435\u0441\u0435\u0447\u0458\u0435"],t.s)
B.b2u=new A.d('Mars holds a unique position: it is the first planet with an orbit external to Earth\'s. Its cycle is significantly longer than the annual cycle of the Earth/Sun (related to basic survival and conscious goal-setting) and the cycles of the inner planets (Mercury and Venus, responsible for short-term processes and personal desires). This positions Mars as a principle associated with the active manifestation of will in the external world, requiring medium-term planning and directed effort.\n\nIf the Earth/Sun is consciousness and the will to live, and Venus is personal desires and values, then Mars represents the "principle of active action" aimed at achieving these desires and protecting one\'s interests in the external environment. This correlates with:\n\nThe instinct for self-preservation and protection: Active measures to defend one\'s boundaries, interests, and physical safety. This can manifest as determination, courage, assertiveness, and in extreme cases, as aggression or conflict.\n\nProactivity and initiative: The ability to initiate actions, overcome obstacles, and achieve set goals. This is the principle of "doing" and self-assertion.\n\nPhysical energy and endurance: Mars is associated with bodily strength, the capacity for sustained effort, and competition.\n\nPrimary social interaction (at the level of action): Although the cycle of Mars is not yet long enough to be responsible for complex social structures (like Jupiter\'s), it already has a social aspect. This is manifested in the need to cooperate to achieve common goals (e.g., in a team or group), to compete, or to protect "one\'s own."\n\nEvents and processes associated with the Mars cycle (1-2 years) often require consistent effort, skill development, and the ability to withstand pressure for several months or even up to a couple of years. This corresponds to projects that require active implementation, overcoming resistance, or mastering new areas of activity.',null,B.b,null,null)
B.atV=s([B.b2u],t.n)
