B.b0K=new A.d("Pluto, also invisible to the naked eye, marks the slowest of the known stable rhythms. Its role is determined not by its mass, but by its unique orbital resonance with Neptune, which makes it a key marker of dynamics at the farthest reaches of the system.\n\nIts principle is not so much the conscious destruction of outdated systems (which is closer to Uranus), but an instinctive, cleansing reaction of the [Field]'s organism to what has become non-viable and toxic under the influence of Neptune's slow currents. This is a crisis that comes not from the mind, but from the very depths of the survival instinct.\n\nThe extremely slow and uneven cycle of Pluto (about 248 years) marks the rhythm of transformation of deep socio-psychological structures that have existed for several generations. This is not the cycle of the evolution of civilization as a whole, but rather the life cycle of its fundamental, often unspoken, attitudes towards power, collective resources, and survival.",null,B.b,null,null)
