B.aTt=new A.d(' is derived from its position as the first planet beyond the orbit of Saturn\u2014the marker of structure, tradition, and established boundaries. Uranus logically symbolizes "that which is beyond": the principle of transgression, deviation from the norm, and the striving for freedom from existing frameworks.\n\nIts active cycle phase (~42 years) perfectly corresponds to the period of active social and creative life of one generation. Conventionally, this is the time from when a generation begins to form its own values, distinct from their parents\' (around 20-25 years old), to the moment it becomes the "older generation" itself and passes the baton to the next (around 60-65 years old).\n\nThus, Uranus marks not so much personal rebellions as generational cycles of renewal: the process by which a new generation creates and implements its alternative systems, ideas, and lifestyles that "hack" the established order of the previous generation.',null,B.b,null,null)
